  <Item id="2fe7b0eb-de52-59a1-b25f-68cef26656a0" type="Default">
    <Attribute name="Contents">
      <Value>
        <Paragraph>
          <Text bold="true" font-size="+40%">Concept of the UoO — Rear PTO control system</Text>
        </Paragraph>
        <Paragraph>Unit of observation per ISO 25119-2:2018, Clause 5. Machine: Ager Dynamics T6100 tractor platform (82–125 kW). The UoO is the E/E/PES part of the rear PTO control: PTO-ECU 200 with its sensors, operator controls and the clutch valve output stage. The wet clutch pack, spring-applied PTO brake, gearbox and stub shaft are mechanical context — their failures are outside ISO 25119 scope but appear in the FTA as context events.</Paragraph>
      </Value>
    </Attribute>
    <Attribute name="Type" value="5" />
    <Attribute name="ID">
      <Value>PTO-UOO-000</Value>
    </Attribute>
    <Attribute name="Status" value="2" />
  </Item>
  <Item id="4215a5b7-7131-511a-8692-e6bf744d21a8" type="Default">
    <Attribute name="Contents">
      <Value>
        <Paragraph>
          <Text bold="true" font-size="+16%">1. System overview</Text>
        </Paragraph>
        <Paragraph alignment="Center"><Image width="980.00" height="560.00"></Image></Paragraph>
        <Paragraph alignment="Center"><Text italic="true">Figure 1 — UoO boundary and actuation context</Text></Paragraph>
      </Value>
    </Attribute>
    <Attribute name="Type" value="1" />
    <Attribute name="ID">
      <Value>PTO-UOO-001</Value>
    </Attribute>
    <Attribute name="Status" value="2" />
  </Item>
  <Item id="565e8605-7f4b-50fe-a161-24cc39769e3e" type="Default">
    <Attribute name="Contents">
      <Value>
        <Paragraph>
          <Text bold="true" font-size="+16%">2. Functions of the UoO</Text>
        </Paragraph>
        <Paragraph>F1 Engage/disengage the rear PTO on operator command (cab switch).</Paragraph>
        <Paragraph>F2 External engage jog from either fender (coupling aid, hold-to-run).</Paragraph>
        <Paragraph>F3 Select and supervise the PTO speed mode (540 / 540E / 1000 rpm).</Paragraph>
        <Paragraph>F4 Automatic shut-off on operator-presence loss during mobile work; stationary-mode exception with deliberate confirmation.</Paragraph>
        <Paragraph>F5 Controlled engagement ramp (limit driveline shock).</Paragraph>
        <Paragraph>F6 Status indication to the cluster (lamp, buzzer) — QM.</Paragraph>
        <Paragraph>Historical basis: the function set and its safety behaviour follow common European tractor practice and the machine-level requirements of ISO 26322 / ISO 4254-1 for PTO controls.</Paragraph>
      </Value>
    </Attribute>
    <Attribute name="Type" value="1" />
    <Attribute name="ID">
      <Value>PTO-UOO-002</Value>
    </Attribute>
    <Attribute name="Status" value="2" />
  </Item>
  <Item id="0970b6e7-f6cc-531a-9605-87fe439669f9" type="Default">
    <Attribute name="Contents">
      <Value>
        <Paragraph>
          <Text bold="true" font-size="+16%">3. Limits and interfaces</Text>
        </Paragraph>
        <Table><Column width="190.00"/><Column width="80.00"/><Column width="130.00"/><Column width="260.00"/><Row><Cell><Paragraph alignment="Center"><Text bold="true">Interface</Text></Paragraph></Cell><Cell><Paragraph alignment="Center"><Text bold="true">Direction</Text></Paragraph></Cell><Cell><Paragraph alignment="Center"><Text bold="true">Type</Text></Paragraph></Cell><Cell><Paragraph alignment="Center"><Text bold="true">Characteristics</Text></Paragraph></Cell></Row><Row><Cell><Paragraph alignment="Left"><Text>Cab PTO switch</Text></Paragraph></Cell><Cell><Paragraph alignment="Left"><Text>in</Text></Paragraph></Cell><Cell><Paragraph alignment="Left"><Text>2 × discrete</Text></Paragraph></Cell><Cell><Paragraph alignment="Left"><Text>lift-collar guarded rocker; NO + NC contacts, 12 V wetted</Text></Paragraph></Cell></Row><Row><Cell><Paragraph alignment="Left"><Text>Fender buttons L / R</Text></Paragraph></Cell><Cell><Paragraph alignment="Left"><Text>in</Text></Paragraph></Cell><Cell><Paragraph alignment="Left"><Text>discrete</Text></Paragraph></Cell><Cell><Paragraph alignment="Left"><Text>momentary, guarded housing, hold-to-run only</Text></Paragraph></Cell></Row><Row><Cell><Paragraph alignment="Left"><Text>Operator presence (seat)</Text></Paragraph></Cell><Cell><Paragraph alignment="Left"><Text>in</Text></Paragraph></Cell><Cell><Paragraph alignment="Left"><Text>discrete ×2</Text></Paragraph></Cell><Cell><Paragraph alignment="Left"><Text>seat switch, second contact for plausibility</Text></Paragraph></Cell></Row><Row><Cell><Paragraph alignment="Left"><Text>Speed-mode selector</Text></Paragraph></Cell><Cell><Paragraph alignment="Left"><Text>in</Text></Paragraph></Cell><Cell><Paragraph alignment="Left"><Text>analog coded</Text></Paragraph></Cell><Cell><Paragraph alignment="Left"><Text>540 / 540E / 1000, resistor-coded lever position</Text></Paragraph></Cell></Row><Row><Cell><Paragraph alignment="Left"><Text>PTO shaft speed</Text></Paragraph></Cell><Cell><Paragraph alignment="Left"><Text>in</Text></Paragraph></Cell><Cell><Paragraph alignment="Left"><Text>frequency</Text></Paragraph></Cell><Cell><Paragraph alignment="Left"><Text>inductive pickup on 58-tooth wheel, 0.3–3 kHz</Text></Paragraph></Cell></Row><Row><Cell><Paragraph alignment="Left"><Text>Engine speed (CAN)</Text></Paragraph></Cell><Cell><Paragraph alignment="Left"><Text>in</Text></Paragraph></Cell><Cell><Paragraph alignment="Left"><Text>CAN 250k</Text></Paragraph></Cell><Cell><Paragraph alignment="Left"><Text>J1939 EEC1, 20 ms cycle, timeout supervised</Text></Paragraph></Cell></Row><Row><Cell><Paragraph alignment="Left"><Text>Clutch valve</Text></Paragraph></Cell><Cell><Paragraph alignment="Left"><Text>out</Text></Paragraph></Cell><Cell><Paragraph alignment="Left"><Text>PWM 12 V</Text></Paragraph></Cell><Cell><Paragraph alignment="Left"><Text>solenoid 2.2 Ω; de-energised = clutch OPEN (brake applied)</Text></Paragraph></Cell></Row><Row><Cell><Paragraph alignment="Left"><Text>Valve current sense</Text></Paragraph></Cell><Cell><Paragraph alignment="Left"><Text>in</Text></Paragraph></Cell><Cell><Paragraph alignment="Left"><Text>analog</Text></Paragraph></Cell><Cell><Paragraph alignment="Left"><Text>shunt + amplifier, 0–2 A, read by both MCUs</Text></Paragraph></Cell></Row><Row><Cell><Paragraph alignment="Left"><Text>Clutch pressure switch</Text></Paragraph></Cell><Cell><Paragraph alignment="Left"><Text>in</Text></Paragraph></Cell><Cell><Paragraph alignment="Left"><Text>discrete</Text></Paragraph></Cell><Cell><Paragraph alignment="Left"><Text>closes ≥ 14 bar (clutch filled), plausibility only</Text></Paragraph></Cell></Row><Row><Cell><Paragraph alignment="Left"><Text>Cluster indication</Text></Paragraph></Cell><Cell><Paragraph alignment="Left"><Text>out</Text></Paragraph></Cell><Cell><Paragraph alignment="Left"><Text>CAN 250k</Text></Paragraph></Cell><Cell><Paragraph alignment="Left"><Text>PTO state lamp + buzzer request (QM function)</Text></Paragraph></Cell></Row></Table>
      </Value>
    </Attribute>
    <Attribute name="Type" value="1" />
    <Attribute name="ID">
      <Value>PTO-UOO-003</Value>
    </Attribute>
    <Attribute name="Status" value="2" />
  </Item>
  <Item id="5c8162ef-dca7-56fd-abcb-b97b983225cc" type="Default">
    <Attribute name="Contents">
      <Value>
        <Paragraph>
          <Text bold="true" font-size="+16%">4. Ambient conditions and sources of stress (5.3.3)</Text>
        </Paragraph>
        <Paragraph>Environment class per ISO 15003: cab-mounted ECU, −25 °C … +70 °C ambient, vibration 5 g (10–500 Hz), humidity 95 % non-condensing, IP54 at the connector zone. Electrical: 12 V system, cranking dips to 6 V, load dump per ISO 7637-2 pulse 5a (clamped), reverse polarity −14 V. EMC per ISO 14982 (agricultural machinery).</Paragraph>
        <Paragraph>Stress sources considered: interaction with the hitch ECU (shared CAN), chemical exposure (fertiliser dust, washing), operator misuse (jump start, welding on frame), harness chafing near the fender buttons, and assembly errors (connector cross-mating is excluded by keying — fault exclusion FE-1, justified in the FMEA).</Paragraph>
        <Paragraph alignment="Center"><Image width="900.00" height="340.00"></Image></Paragraph>
        <Paragraph alignment="Center"><Text italic="true">Figure 2 — mission profile used for the IEC/TR 62380 reliability prediction (SafeFIT)</Text></Paragraph>
      </Value>
    </Attribute>
    <Attribute name="Type" value="1" />
    <Attribute name="ID">
      <Value>PTO-UOO-004</Value>
    </Attribute>
    <Attribute name="Status" value="2" />
  </Item>
  <Item id="06245e51-0370-5113-aeda-28cda1d8f28a" type="Default">
    <Attribute name="Contents">
      <Value>
        <Paragraph>
          <Text bold="true" font-size="+16%">5. Additional determinations (5.3.4)</Text>
        </Paragraph>
        <Paragraph>New development: the PTO-ECU 200 replaces the relay-based PTO control of the T5 series (field history 11 years, 41 000 units — used as proven-in-use reference for the valve and clutch, not for the new electronics). Reliability input data: IEC/TR 62380 with the mission profile of Figure 2. Tools: SafeSuite (this project), SafeFIT (FIT prediction), SafeFMEA, SafeTree (FTA). Staff qualification per Safety Plan §2.</Paragraph>
      </Value>
    </Attribute>
    <Attribute name="Type" value="1" />
    <Attribute name="ID">
      <Value>PTO-UOO-005</Value>
    </Attribute>
    <Attribute name="Status" value="2" />
  </Item>
</StructuredDocument>
